# L §2.3 `price = ref | "last" "(" ref ")"` after `priced` on the kind's place line
# and the place section; L §5.10 Value: "A price that is a reading (a valuation) is named with its carry, `priced
# last(val)` (§4.6), on the kind, the place or the entry, and `value` reads it so; a plain `priced
# val` reads it as any reading is read, a hole on a day with no reading"; L §5.7: `priced p` "values a place whose
# single position is valued by the price input p" (assets: "value = v at d, from valuation readings"). val has one
# reading, 500 000.00 PLN at 2026-03-01. a1: flat (plain `priced val`) on the reading's day: 500 000 PLN. a2: the next
# day, no reading: HOLE-NOREADING (L §4.6, §8.1 "<x>[k] has no reading at <instant>"). a3: flat2 `priced last(val)`
# carries it: 500 000 PLN. a4: house, of the kind `homes ... priced last(val)`, carries the reading
# of 2026-03-01 on 2026-03-02 (writer 8: `within` and HOLE-STALE are gone, L §2.3). a5: on 2026-03-01 it is 500 000 PLN.
# value multiplies exactly and doesn't round (L §5.10), so it prints as a num PLN.
=== pr.tally
model pr
  tally 2
  on 2026-06-30
  start 2026-01-01
  end 2026-12-31

source s "synthetic"
unit PLN: currency minor 0.01
unit etf "fund unit"

kind homes: place PLN min 0 priced last(val)

place flat: assets PLN priced val lives 2026-01-01..
place flat2: assets PLN priced last(val) lives 2026-01-01..
place house: homes lives 2026-01-01..
place world: outside lives 2026-01-01..
place konto: accounts PLN lives 2026-01-01..

input val: money PLN reading
input age: int
input px: num PLN/etf reading
input day: date

move buy: transfers
  on day
  leg cash from world to konto amount 0 PLN

ask a1: value(flat, 2026-03-01) in PLN law 2026-06-30
ask a2: value(flat, 2026-03-02) in PLN law 2026-06-30
ask a3: value(flat2, 2026-03-02) in PLN law 2026-06-30
ask a4: value(house, 2026-03-02) in PLN law 2026-06-30
ask a5: value(house, 2026-03-01) in PLN law 2026-06-30

version v1
  cite s
  governs always
  known 2026-01-01
  val = 500 000.00 PLN at 2026-03-01 "wycena"
  age = 0 "own"
  day = 2026-02-01 "own"
  opening[konto] = 0 PLN at 2026-01-01 start "own"
=== expect
a1: 500 000 PLN
  law date 2026-06-30, cut 2026-06-30
a2: ?"val has no reading at 2026-03-02" (val)
  law date 2026-06-30, cut 2026-06-30
a3: 500 000 PLN
  law date 2026-06-30, cut 2026-06-30
a4: 500 000 PLN
  law date 2026-06-30, cut 2026-06-30
a5: 500 000 PLN
  law date 2026-06-30, cut 2026-06-30
